    "user_message": [
      "A beautiful winter evening scene in Vilnius, Lithuania. The composition looks down a cozy Old Town street blanketed in fresh white snow, leading the eye toward Cathedral Square where the white bell tower is partially visible, frosted with snow. On the hill beyond, the iconic red-brick Gediminas Tower rises above snow-covered trees. Historic baroque architecture frames the street: ornate facades with pilasters, stucco details, and colorful pastel walls peeking through the snow. Warm golden lights glow from windows and doorways, and classic street lamps cast a soft amber haze on the snowy ground. Gentle snowflakes fall through a crisp blue-hour sky, with subtle reflections on snow-dusted cobblestones. Traditional Lithuanian architectural motifs\u2014decorative cornices, arched doorways, wrought-iron balconies\u2014are visible despite the snow coverage. Atmosphere is serene and inviting, realistic and detailed, with balanced lighting and soft shadows."
